<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculate the corrected mean and standard deviation values (STACK)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>
A scientist is weighing each of {@N@} fish. She obtains a mean of
{@m@} g and a standard deviation of {@s@} g.
After completing the weighing, she finds that the scale was misaligned,
and always under-reported every weight by {@e@} g, i.e. a fish that
really weighed {@x@} g was reported to weigh {@x_reported@} g.
</p>

<p>
What is the mean and standard deviation after correcting for the error
in the scale?
</p>

<p>
[Hint: recall that the mean measures central tendency and the standard
deviation measures spread.]
</p>

<p>
Corrected mean: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] g [[feedback:prt1]]
</p>

<p>
Corrected standard deviation: [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] g [[feedback:prt2]]
</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>
The scale under-reported every weight by {@e@} g, so {@e@} g must be added to each recorded weight.
Therefore, the corrected mean is
\[
{@m@}+{@e@}={@ta1@}\text{ g}.
\]
</p>

<p>
Adding the same value to every observation shifts all the weights by the same amount but does not change their spread.
Therefore, the standard deviation remains unchanged:
\[
{@ta2@}\text{ g}.
\]
</p>

<p>
Hence, the corrected mean is {@ta1@} g and the corrected standard deviation is {@ta2@} g.
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
